In a non-uniform electric field, the unequal electric fields at the locations of $+q$ and $-q$ result in unequal forces ($F_+ 
eq F_-$), creating a non-zero net translational force $\vec{F}_{	ext{net}} 
eq 0$. In general, a net torque $\vec{	au} = \vec{p} 	imes \vec{E} 
eq 0$ is also experienced.
